  "demographics": {
    "age": 55,
    "sex": "F",
    "ethnicity_or_context": "adult woman treated in Poland; vaccination status not reported"
  },
  "presentation_summary": [
    "55-year-old woman presented with fever, fatigue, arthralgia, myalgia, dyspnea, dysphonia, sore throat, cough, and erythematous rash.",
    "Physical examination showed generalized maculopapular skin rash, Koplik spots, conjunctivitis, and basal pulmonary crepitations.",
    "Blood tests showed leukopenia, lymphopenia, thrombocytopenia, elevated AST, ALT, GGT, creatine kinase, and mildly elevated CRP.",
    "Influenza, HBV, HIV 1/2, and Legionella tests were negative.",
    "Measles was confirmed by positive IgM and by measles PCR in oral swab and urine.",
    "CT of the lungs and CT of the brain were unremarkable.",
    "After initial improvement, she developed cognitive dysfunction with impaired daily organization, difficulty dressing, and loss of spontaneous communication despite ability to answer simple direct questions.",
    "CSF was normal, CSF measles PCR and multiplex meningitis or encephalitis PCR were negative, and brain MRI, ECG, and EEG were normal.",
    "The treating team suspected chronic encephalopathy and organized rehabilitation."
  ],
